# Tailwind CSS Standards

Related: [react-typescript.mdc](react-typescript.mdc) (components), [front-end-structure.mdc](front-end-structure.mdc) (file layout).

## Core Principles

- Use Tailwind utility classes for component styling.
- Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS.
- Avoid custom CSS files unless absolutely necessary.
- Never use inline styles.
- Never use the `@apply` directive.
- Follow a mobile-first approach.
- Prioritize readable and maintainable class lists.

Preferred:

```tsx
<div className="flex items-center gap-4 rounded-lg border p-4" />
```

Avoid:

```tsx
<div className="user-card" />
```

## Utility Classes

- Use spacing, sizing, typography, color, border, and layout utilities directly.
- Prefer composing existing utilities over creating ad-hoc custom class names.
- Keep class names concise and consistently ordered.

## Responsive Design

- Design mobile-first.
- Add responsive variants with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, `2xl:`.
- Avoid fixed layouts that do not adapt across viewports.

Preferred:

```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" />
```

## Class Ordering

Maintain this order when practical:

1. Layout (`flex`, `grid`, `block`)
2. Position (`relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`)
3. Size (`w-*`, `h-*`, `min-w-*`, `max-w-*`)
4. Spacing (`p-*`, `px-*`, `py-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`)
5. Typography (`text-*`, `font-*`, `leading-*`)
6. Visual (`bg-*`, `border-*`, `rounded-*`, `shadow-*`)
7. State (`hover:*`, `focus:*`, `active:*`, `disabled:*`)
8. Responsive (`sm:*`, `md:*`, `lg:*`, `xl:*`, `2xl:*`)

Example:

```tsx
className="
flex items-center
w-full
gap-4 px-4 py-2
text-sm font-medium
bg-background border rounded-md
hover:bg-accent
md:px-6
"
```

## Colors

- Use semantic color tokens from the Tailwind theme.
- Avoid hardcoded hex values in class names.

Preferred:

```tsx
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground border-border" />
```

Avoid:

```tsx
<div className="bg-[#2563EB] text-[#FFFFFF] border-[#D1D5DB]" />
```

## Spacing

- Use the Tailwind spacing scale.
- Avoid arbitrary values unless there is a strong, documented reason.

Preferred:

```tsx
<div className="p-4 gap-6 mt-8" />
```

Avoid:

```tsx
<div className="p-[17px] gap-[13px]" />
```

## Typography

- Use Tailwind typography utilities and consistent design-system sizes.
- Avoid arbitrary font sizes and weights.

Preferred:

```tsx
<p className="text-sm text-base text-lg font-medium" />
```

Avoid:

```tsx
<p className="text-[15px] font-[550]" />
```

## Design Tokens

- Define and maintain colors, spacing, typography, radii, shadows, and animation in `tailwind.config.ts`.
- Reuse theme tokens and avoid repeating hardcoded design values.

## shadcn/ui Integration

- Use shadcn/ui components whenever available.
- Prefer component variants before custom styling.
- Avoid modifying generated shadcn/ui source files unless task-scoped and necessary.

## Styling Checklist

Before submitting code:

- Uses Tailwind utility classes
- No unnecessary custom CSS
- No inline styles
- No `@apply` usage
- Mobile responsive behavior implemented
- Uses theme tokens
- No hardcoded colors
- No excessive arbitrary values
- Follows class ordering convention
- Reuses existing shadcn/ui components when applicable

## Verification

```bash
cd front-end
npm run type-check
npm run lint
```
